WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.240
Netflix is constantly churning out high-quality
entertainment, but there's so much of it in

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.050
the works that it can be hard to keep track
of what's ahead.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:12.140
Here are some of the most intriguing upcoming
Netflix originals to get pumped about.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.000
After decades of delighting the world with
his manic Muppets, Jim Henson and his progressive

00:00:17.009 --> 00:00:22.259
partners in puppetry released the dazzling
and ambitious The Dark Crystal in 1982.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:27.150
This serious, hardcore fantasy epic with shades
of Tolkien focused on mythical races vying

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.700
for control of a powerful gem that keeps order
in the universe.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.820
"This is a piece of the dark crystal!"

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.060
It was a box office hit and a cult classic
and now Netflix is revisiting it.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.920
The Dark Crystal: Age of Resistance will be
a prequel series, set long before the events

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.920
of the film, relying on old school puppetry
instead of CGI.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.910
There's no hard release date yet, but expect
the Age of Resistance to hit the streaming

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.240
service sometime before 2020.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.960
The breakout star of one of the most popular
and critically acclaimed sci-fi TV shows of

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:02.710
all time is making her way back to a space-set
series.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:07.730
Katee Sackhoff, aka Starbuck from the Battlestar
Galactica reboot, has signed on to star in

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.770
an upcoming Netflix thriller called Another
Life.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.659
In this dark science-fiction drama that sounds
like equal parts Alien and The Orville, Sackhoff

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:20.899
stars as Niko Breckinridge, an astronaut who
leads a crew on a spooky trip to explore the

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:24.560
origins of an important artifact of an alien
civilization.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.240
Another Life boasts a notable pedigree: it's
produced by Halfire Entertainment, the company

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.720
that made Netflix's acclaimed adaptation of
Margaret Atwood's Alias Grace.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.800
There's room enough in the infinite expanse
of Netflix for another show about the infinite

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.409
expanse of space.

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:45.979
Like Another Life, Away is a show about astronauts,
but this one is much more grounded in reality.

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:51.549
Based in part on Chris Jones' 2014 Esquire
article of the same name about astronaut Scott

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:56.689
Kelly, the drama is about Emma Green, a fictional
American astronaut struggling with leaving

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:00.789
her family behind for her one-year trip into
the wild black yonder.

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:05.439
Get your tissues ready: Away is probably going
to be a tearjerker, because of the man behind

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:10.300
it: It's the co-creation of Jason Katims,
the mastermind behind beloved TV weepfests

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.240
Friday Night Lights and Parenthood.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.560
The King Arthur legends have been part of
the cultural fabric of England for well over

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:21.890
a thousand years, and these legends get adapted
into movies and TV shows with regularity because

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:26.730
people know and love them… and also because
they're squarely in the public domain.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.170
Legendary graphic novel creator Frank Miller
will publish his own take, told from the point

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.870
of view of the Lady of the Lake.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:38.209
Cursed won't hit bookstores until late 2019,
but Netflix has already recognized the pull

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:42.470
of the material, and put a serialized version
of the book into production starring Katherine

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:47.340
Langford, best known for anchoring the service's
controversial hit 13 Reasons Why.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.720
Visionary filmmaker Guillermo del Toro is
a beloved fixture of the horror-fantasy genre,

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:57.200
with a filmography that runs from dark fable
Pan's Labyrinth to his more recent hit The

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.200
Shape of Water.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.640
Thanks to a deal with Netflix, del Toro will
revisit his roots in the scary filmmaking

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.500
he so obviously loves.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.110
With the success of Netflix's own Black Mirror,
unsettling anthology series are back in a

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.730
way not seen since the heyday of The Twilight
Zone in the '60s.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.280
The service wants more, and more scary, so
it's ordered 10 installments of Guillermo

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.810
del Toro Presents 10 After Midnight.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.159
According to Variety, del Toro will produce
the series while also curating the stories

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.800
he wishes to tell, and will personally hire
interesting filmmakers to make those standalone

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:29.480
episodes.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.980
He's also slated to write and direct a few
of the episodes himself.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.420
With shows such as GLOW, Unbreakable Kimmy
Schmidt, and Master of None, Netflix helped

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:42.440
popularized the notion of single-camera, film-like
comedy series.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.340
But Netflix is all things to all people, so
it's also explored the classic sitcom format

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.629
with The Ranch, Fuller House, and soon, No
Good Nick.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:55.700
This three-camera family comedy stars two
very familiar faces: Sean Astin and Melissa

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.700
Joan Hart.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:02.040
They play parents Liz and Ed, a career-oriented
mom and goofy dad who bring into their family

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:07.310
a 13-year-old named Nicole, only to slowly
realize that she's actually a con artist with

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.780
inscrutable goals.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:15.060
From Wet Hot American Summer-quoting comedy
nerds to devoted Ant-Man-loving MCU acolytes,

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:17.269
just about everybody loves Paul Rudd.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:21.130
He's starred in a couple of Netflix original
movies, and he's set to star in his first

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.949
series for the online giant.

00:04:22.949 --> 00:04:27.120
From the mind former Daily Show executive
producer Timothy Greenberg and directed by

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.080
Little Miss Sunshine duo Jonathan Dayton and
Valerie Faris, Rudd's latest Netflix project

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.740
is Living With Yourself.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:38.190
Rudd stars as a man for whom life did not
turn out so well, and so he submits to an

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.639
experimental self-improvement treatment.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:45.840
One problem: His replacement is his newer,
better self… and that's also his new rival.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:51.640
Joe Hill and Gabriel Rodriguez's fantasy/horror
title Locke &amp; Key is one of the most popular

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.139
and well-received comics in recent memory.

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:58.530
Three siblings move into the Massachusetts
home that's been in their family for generations,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:03.060
where they find special keys that give them
all magical and superhuman abilities.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:08.550
Just two years after its first issue hit newsstands
in 2008, Hollywood got to work on an adaptation

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.730
for television.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.750
And it's been in the works ever since.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:16.581
Hill will write on the 10-episode series,
while Carlton Cuse of Lost is onboard as a

00:05:16.581 --> 00:05:17.610
producer and developer.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.480
Scandal's Darby Stanchfield is attached to
star.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:25.840
Netflix has blossomed into such an entertainment
juggernaut that it's able to attract and more

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:30.699
than decently compensate content creators
from the world of traditional television.

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:36.069
The latest is prolific writer/director/producer
Ryan Murphy, who helped make FX into a prestige

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:40.699
channel, drawing huge ratings and winning
tons of Emmys for American Horror Story and

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:42.620
American Crime Story.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.099
Netflix offered Murphy $300 million the most
lucrative producer contract in TV history

00:05:48.099 --> 00:05:50.660
to do whatever he wants on the streaming platform.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:56.169
The first of what will likely be many Ryan
Murphy series feels very on-brand: Ratched,

00:05:56.169 --> 00:06:00.600
a prequel series to the classic film and novel
One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:04.020
"I want that television set turned on right
now!"

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.920
It focuses on Nurse Ratched, the no-nonsense
nurse played by Louise Fletcher in the 1975

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.830
movie version of Ken Kesey's book.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:16.470
Frequent Murphy collaborator Sarah Paulson
will take over the role for the series.

